{
  "about": "One fixture for the PGS overlay's seek, tick and manifest-response decisions, read by the Android JVM suite (PGSOverlayTest) and both Apple test targets (AppleClientTests). Windows are [lower_ms, upper_exclusive_ms] in source time, or null. The loaded window in most seek cases is what windowAt(100000) gives: look-behind 5 s, look-ahead 90 s, so its last 20 s (the refresh margin) starts at 170000. seek_cases: `refresh` is whether a seek starts a window load on both clients (Apple's seek and Android's discontinuity apply the same rule, with any failure backoff ended by the seek); `window` is the window that serves the new position (the one to load, the one loading, or the one loaded); `clear_now` is Android's alone, because Apple's cues are timed layers and cannot go stale. tick_cases: whether Apple's 1 s tick, or any Android player event that is not a seek, starts a load; a load covering the position is never replaced, and after window_failures consecutive failures the retry waits 5 s, then 30 s, then stops until a seek. docs/clients/PGS-SUBTITLE-START-PATH-RCA-AND-PLAN.md §5.4, B3 and B4.",
